+## 12. 5D2C2 inactive committed-receipt descriptor
+
+### Bounded data contract
+
+`src/checkpoint_receipts.py` defines the frozen `universe.committed-native-receipt-chain/1` projection and a versioned `universe.committed-native-rebinding-plan/1`. The supported source is an authenticated, same-process committed inspection of exactly one or two consecutive boundaries in a transactional Encounter. The committed receipt Actions are exact native Run/Spot families. The descriptor includes stable Universe, Encounter, Being, Action and Choice IDs; exact integer/binary64 numeric tags; native Action declarations and outcomes; ordered boundary, Action and effect references; supported effect payloads; Target-owned candidate state/history (including legitimate simultaneous `BatchSkillUse`); start-fence data; committed Choice membership; accepted wholly-future Run/Spot choice descriptors; and caller-owned private RNG cursor state under the explicit `exclusive_encounter` ownership assertion.
+
+The projection is a nested tuple data tree, not a file format. It contains no receipt authenticity token, weak reference, process address, Action/Target anchor, Python class/function, callable or mutable native object. It preserves issuer effect order and each Action's causal effect references. It preserves Target-owned results as Target candidate records; it does not derive an Action's experience, damage or HP changes from aggregate Target state. Validation cross-checks Action/effect/lifecycle/Choice references, Run/Spot declarations, awareness/practice recipient and skill links, Target incoming/outgoing links, Target-owned practice exercises, chronology, schemas, and accepted future choice IDs.
+
+Capture requires the existing transactional ownership access protocol, a caller quiescence assertion, an exact private `RNGCursor`, an explicit exclusive-Encounter scope assertion, fresh authentic receipts, complete Target history, and no known shared cursor. These checks do not prove the absence of arbitrary external aliases; the host still attests that no other owner writes the cursor or Encounter during capture.
+
+### Reconstruction and rebinding obligations
+
+The companion plan lists logical Entity, Action and Choice IDs, committed boundary sequence, and these required future stages: select compatible rule/adapter versions; allocate new native objects; bind each ID uniquely; rebuild only whitelisted Run/Spot declarations; revalidate Target-owned practice and chronological receipt coverage; reconstruct the ChoiceBook and private RNG cursor under exclusive ownership; regenerate process-local Action/Target/storage anchors from rebound objects; and authenticate/register new receipts only after the complete candidate passes validation. The plan records obligations only. No object allocation, receipt reissuance, authenticity registration, checkpoint export/import, replay or restore is implemented. Receipt authenticity must not be copied across processes or inferred from descriptor content.
+
+### Explicitly unsupported and readiness
+
+The descriptor rejects unsupported Action/effect families; active pending, executing, cancelled or incomplete choices; missing, stale, duplicate, forged or out-of-order receipts; nonconsecutive or longer histories; non-Being Target records; incomplete Target history; objective Reality/history constraints; observer evidence, Belief and testimony; personal-history-bound practice (`history_revision`); custom callbacks; unknown schema fields/versions; and ambiguous/shared RNG ownership. It also refuses when receipt/Target causal links do not close. These are bounded adapter exclusions, not new simulation rules.
+
+This descriptor does not resolve the broader 5D2B semantic/alias closure gaps or prove durable definition and entity reconstruction. `receipt_rebinding_required` remains in checkpoint diagnostics. `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false, and `require_complete()` plus all existing transactional serialization/restoration refusals remain unchanged. A subsequent increment would need separately authorized allocation/rebinding and issuance semantics, freshness/identity guarantees, failure safety, and continuation tests before any readiness claim.
+
+## 13. 5D2C3 bounded Run/Spot semantic field closure
+
+### Local certificate and declared subset
+
+Native inventory mode may include `native.run-spot-field-closure/1` plus the diagnostic `bounded_run_spot_closure_verified`. This is a **local field/dependency proof**, never a checkpoint readiness flag. It covers one exact Universe/Library/Encounter graph with a selected Encounter whose participant and referenced entity IDs resolve uniquely to exact registered Beings; no other registered object, non-Being participant, pending/cancelled Action, external recipient binding, unsupported event, or more than two committed receipt boundaries; exact Run/Spot accepted choices; the 5D2C2 authenticated receipt descriptor; and a private caller-owned `RNGCursor`. Capture does not execute callbacks, roll RNG, or mutate the graph. The existing portable choice and receipt descriptors provide the Action, reservation, lifecycle, chronology, effect, Target-history and accepted-future-choice coverage.
+
+### A/D/T/U classification
+
+| Classification | Bounded native Run/Spot treatment |
+|---|---|
+| **A — authoritative** | Universe ID/name, Library logical ID, Encounter participants/queues/clock and current scheduling state; the complete exact registered BeingDefinition rows needed by participating Beings; the native SkillDictionary rows (including `run` and `spot`); each selected Being's logical ID, original/current definitions, spatial and Q/B state, skill ranks, practice, and Target-owned history where committed; plus portable accepted choices and committed receipts through 5D2C1/5D2C2. |
+| **D — derived/reissued** | Native class tags; accepted-choice signatures are not copied and must be regenerated from fresh destination objects; receipt/Target/Action/storage authenticity anchors must be freshly rebound and reissued only after full future restore validation. The existing live signatures and receipt issuer are unchanged. |
+| **T — transient** | Universe/ChoiceBook locks, active ownership leases, live boundary/dispatch state, and process-local identity/authenticity data. Fresh synchronization and runtime anchors are future restore work. |
+| **U — outside this proof** | Other Library dictionaries and their semantic definitions; `BeingDictionary.object_categories`; non-Being world objects; unrelated group/formation/conditional state; Belief/testimony/external recipients; Reality additions and personal-history constraints; unsupported Action/event/callback families; unreviewed instance overrides and aliases outside selected Being current definitions. Their presence cannot become checkpoint readiness from this local certificate. |
+
+`src/checkpoint_fields.py` supplies the exact A/D/T/U vocabulary for the bounded owner types, and the adapter verifies that those classifications partition each corresponding closed-field adapter. BeingDictionary entries must be exact BeingDefinitions keyed by their matching `obj_type`; every selected Being's `original` must be that exact shared Library definition. Current BeingDefinitions are detached from their originals, exclusive per Being, recursively closed over native data, and may not share mutable subobjects with another Being or Library definition. SkillDictionary entries have the exact `(is_ordinary, is_progressive)` boolean schema and unique mutable row ownership; every selected current rank must resolve to a definition. Logical references must resolve by exact registered ID. Physiology IDs, when present, must resolve through the exact Encounter registry; Q/B remain frozen data and no fatigue settlement is activated.
+
+The native optional-value contract permits missing pre-first-commit Target-history storage or a list validated against receipts; `spatial_state` may be `None` or exact native SpatialState; geometry and visual occlusion may be absent or exact native values; physiology ID may be absent or registered. `personal_history` must be `None` for this subset. Instance-level `alignment` and `current_armor_class` overrides refuse because their legacy storage/consumer semantics are not part of the Run/Spot contract. Required definition and skill fields are checked for exact types and finite numeric values; unknown fields, malformed dictionaries, dangling identities, wrong original-definition bindings, mutable sharing and stale recaptures refuse or produce an explicit `bounded_run_spot_closure_refused` diagnostic.
+
+`BeingDictionary.object_categories` is deliberately classified U: `Library.load_library()` currently calls `self.being_dictionary.load_object_categories(categories_filename)` for the object category file, and those category members are not necessarily BeingDefinition keys (for example, ordinary Object names). This local Run/Spot proof does not reinterpret or repair that existing contract. Whole-checkpoint `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false; `semantic_closure_adapter_incomplete`, `receipt_rebinding_required`, and all export/restore refusals remain. No file schema, receipt issuance, restoration, replay, or live integration is implemented.
+
+## 14. 5D2C4 inactive bounded Run/Spot envelope
+
+`src/checkpoint_envelope.py` composes one coordinated `NativeInventory` capture into the frozen in-memory `universe.native-run-spot-checkpoint-envelope/1` candidate. Its authoritative state is the complete detached native inventory tree from that capture; explicit sections identify the 5D2C3 field-closure certificate, accepted future Run/Spot choice descriptors, zero-to-two committed receipt boundaries and their chain descriptor, current private caller-owned RNGCursor state, compatibility fingerprint, root logical IDs, diagnostics, and reconstruction obligations. Choice/receipt/certificate sections are cross-checked against that same state tree. The source inventory performs coordinated ownership, read-set and compatibility checks before returning; envelope assembly does not reread the Universe or stitch captures from different revisions. Numeric values retain the existing exact integer/binary64 tags, ordered collections remain ordered, and the envelope contains only detached data values and tuples.
+
+`bounded_envelope_validated` is an explicit local status for successful assembly and same-process freshness validation. The content digest detects candidate edits but is not an authenticity seal. The validator requires the exact issued in-process candidate, checks its digest and internal component closure, then delegates freshness validation to the existing native inventory validator. It does not grant process-independent identity, receipt authenticity, save, restore, or continuation. `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false, and the existing save/export/restore refusals are unchanged.
+
+Future restoration still requires a compatible native allocator; reconstruction of Library/Being/Encounter/ChoiceBook, accepted Action declarations and fresh process-local choice signatures; exact reference/alias rebinding; and authenticated receipt reissuance with regenerated Action, Target, and storage anchors after full validation. The envelope remains limited to the exact 5D2C3 Run/Spot subset. Other Action families, non-Being entities, external recipients, Reality/history additions, custom callbacks, shared/module RNG, unsupported definition dictionaries/categories, multiple Encounters, and unreviewed aliases remain refused or outside the certificate.
