+## 15. 5D2C5 detached Run/Spot wire representation
+
+`src/checkpoint_wire.py` defines `universe.native-run-spot-checkpoint-wire/1`, a strict canonical UTF-8 JSON byte representation of the complete 5D2C4 detached envelope DTO. The top-level object has exactly `schema`, `envelope`, and `sha256`; unknown or duplicate keys refuse. The envelope payload is an ordered array representation of the immutable tuple data, retaining explicit nulls, booleans, absent fields, ordered sequences/maps, logical reference tags, and exact integer/binary64 string tags. Untagged JSON floats, noncanonical number encodings, dangling inventory references, duplicate logical/alias nodes, duplicate map/field keys, unknown native fields/tags, mismatched choice/receipt/effect/Target links, and unsupported families refuse. Encoder/decoder limits are 32 MiB, 128 nesting levels, one million data nodes, one million characters per string, and 4,096 decimal digits per integer.
+
+The payload includes the existing source/rule compatibility fingerprint for inspection. A decoder can read and preserve it, but this wire codec does not establish runtime compatibility or cross-version rule equivalence; a future restore must apply an explicitly reviewed compatibility policy. Version 1 is closed: changing required envelope or field semantics requires a new wire schema version. Version-1 readers reject unknown required fields and tags rather than ignoring them. The SHA-256 digest detects accidental corruption only; it is not an authenticity credential.
+
+`decode_run_spot_wire()` returns a detached `DecodedRunSpotWire` DTO and `reencode_decoded_run_spot_wire()` reproduces canonical bytes in another Python process. The DTO carries no live object, process address, issuance token, receipt seal, or native registry binding. It is not a `NativeRunSpotCheckpointEnvelope` issued by the same-process capture path and cannot satisfy the native freshness validator or authorize receipt use/restoration. The decoder uses the static field vocabulary but does not need the original Universe, Encounter, `checkpoint_inventory` candidate registry, or receipt issuance registry. This establishes only bounded byte-format validity and data round-trip.
+
+Global `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false. File save/load/export, native reconstruction, fresh choice-signature generation, receipt reissuance/authentication, replay, and deterministic continuation remain unimplemented. Existing save/export/restore refusals remain unchanged.
