+## 16. 5D2C6 quarantined initial Run/Spot reconstruction
+
+`src/checkpoint_reconstruction.py` adds `reconstruct_initial_run_spot(DecodedRunSpotWire)`, a developer/test adapter for one exact, zero-committed-boundary Universe/Encounter graph. It repeats strict detached wire validation and requires the current exact implementation/runtime/rule fingerprint, false global readiness flags, the fixed reconstruction-obligation contract, an exclusive caller-owned MT19937 cursor, and the existing 5D2C3 bounded field certificate. A decoded checksum is still only corruption detection; this adapter does not authenticate a world.
+
+The supported initial graph contains the native Universe root (`id="0"`), one Encounter at its original time cursor, the origin Event, one native ChoiceBook, registered BeingInstances and their complete BeingDefinition/SkillDictionary dependencies. The other Library dictionaries must be present as native, empty Action/Armor/Object/Weapon catalogs. Reviewed data-only constructors rebuild the supported Being definitions and their Abilities, Speed, Skills, States, Strategy, Exertion, Q/B, continuous position, Sphere geometry, and VisualOcclusion values. Logical IDs and definition/entity aliases are rebound to newly allocated process objects; constructors must reproduce every captured field exactly. Containment, equipment/body-part ownership, non-Being Objects, physiology profiles/IDs, personal histories, skill-use records, Reality, recipients, callbacks, and nonempty out-of-scope definition catalogs are refused.
+
+Accepted future Run/Spot choices are reconstructed only from `universe.accepted-action-choice/1` descriptors. The adapter creates fresh Action objects, preserves their logical IDs, fractional intervals and declaration data, then uses the ordinary native ChoiceBook schedule/validate/accept path. It compares the rebuilt portable descriptor and prepared schedule with the wire descriptor; the in-process declaration signatures and prepared identity anchors are newly generated and never copied. The current scheduler counter is retained after native acceptance. Unsupported Action families, bad identities, dangling references, stale compatibility, invalid RNG state, or any committed boundary/receipt refuse before a result is returned.
+
+Every successful result is explicitly marked quarantined. The public `QuarantinedReconstruction` exposes a detached immutable `QuarantinedReconstructionView`: stable logical identities, Being state snapshots, accepted Run/Spot declarations and reservations, fractional timing, and private RNG metadata/state. It does not expose native Universe, Encounter, Being, Action, definition, mutable container, or RNG cursor references through supported public fields. The native graph is retained in a process-local weak-keyed private store for future reviewed internal rebinding; this is cooperative API encapsulation, not a security boundary against Python reflection, `__dict__` access, monkeypatching, or malicious private-code access. The existing process-local guards still protect Encounter/Universe gameplay entry points. The graph is not published into an existing Universe and does not authorize save/load, receipt reissuance, replay, or deterministic continuation. Source graphs and module RNG are unchanged; the view contains the exact detached private RNG state. `Library(..., load_definitions=False)` is an opt-in constructor mode used to avoid loading host configuration while building a reviewed Library; existing constructor behavior remains the default.
+
+All three global readiness flags remain false. The support boundary is intentionally initial-only: even valid one- and two-boundary receipt envelopes are refused. Native catalogs beyond the declared Being/Skill subset and unresolved profile or ownership relations remain limitations rather than inferred mappings. Existing transactional serialization and restoration refusals remain in force.
