+## 18. 5D2C8 detached one-boundary Spot projection
+
+`src/checkpoint_projection.py` adds `project_quarantined_spot_boundary(DecodedRunSpotWire)`. It repeats strict version-1 wire validation, then accepts exactly one initial integer boundary, one committed Choice, and one or more exact native Spot Actions sharing the same registered actor and observed Being. It rejects future accepted choices, multiple boundaries, Run/mixed families, any nonzero damage/fatal state, observer evidence or recipient bindings, personal-history-bound practice, unsupported effects, or extra participant Target records.
+
+The return value is `QuarantinedSpotBoundaryProjection/1`, a frozen tree of immutable tuples and scalars with explicit logical IDs. It retains each Action's declaration, outcome, exact tagged start/end values and causal effect references; each typed effect identity/payload; each Target's exact candidate-state data, HP/position, incoming/outgoing effects and awareness; and the committed Choice and private RNG-after data. Target-owned exercises and common before/after transitions remain separate from Action causes. The batch practice row is projected from the Target transition and exercises using the existing `atomic_publication._make_plan()` aggregation that writes `BatchSkillUse`; it does not assign per-Action rank changes or resolve Actions again.
+
+The API is data-only. It allocates no native simulation entities, does not import or consult `atomic_publication` or `Encounter`, does not touch receipt issuance, does not write authoritative histories, and has no progression or native inspection method. Its schema and `quarantined` marker confer no authenticity. The source wire digest remains an integrity check only. Existing `reconstruct_initial_run_spot()` retains the 5D2C7 one-boundary refusal.
+
+The supported example includes two simultaneous Spot Actions by one Being against one observed Being and one shared Target-owned `BatchSkillUse` transition with both causal practice effects. Exact tagged times are preserved without numeric coercion. Future accepted choices are refused by this projection; later boundaries, other Action families, damage, observers/Belief, Reality/history, callbacks, and live fatigue are unsupported. Global `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false. This remains an inactive value projection, not native post-boundary reconstruction or simulation authority.
+
+## 19. 5D2C9B quarantine-only native identity binding
+
+`src/checkpoint_binding.py` adds `bind_quarantined_spot_boundary(decoded, projection=None)` for the exact one-boundary/two-simultaneous-Spot case. It re-encodes and re-decodes the supplied DTO to verify its digest, repeats the 5D2C8 projection, compares any supplied projection exactly, checks the runtime compatibility fingerprint and exclusive caller-cursor RNG, and cross-validates participant Objects, Encounter membership/cursor, finished Action queues, native ChoiceBook membership, action declarations, causal IDs and the single Target-owned batch transition. The accepted Choice is exactly one Choice containing the two projected Spot Actions; future choices, Run/mixed families, extra boundaries/Targets, invalid references, host bindings and unsupported graphs refuse.
+
+The factory uses the reviewed BeingDefinition, BeingInstance and SpotAction constructors to allocate fresh process-local identities with the checkpoint's logical IDs. At 5D2C9B it did not construct an Encounter, accept or register a Choice, insert the Actions into native event/finished queues, execute them, or copy post-boundary practice/history into native history. As extended by 5D2C10 below, the private Being objects carry the exact represented current state while committed Target histories and causal practice remain in the frozen `QuarantinedSpotHistoricalSidecar`, bound by logical IDs. At that stage the private Universe had only its origin Event; section 21 records the later addition of one empty quarantined Encounter Event. The RNG cursor remains private and unchanged.
+
+The public binding exposes only frozen identity/timing views and the detached historical sidecar. The native Universe, Being and Action objects and RNG cursor are retained in a process-local weak-keyed module-private store. Quarantine markers and the direct Action guard keep these shells non-executable through supported APIs. As with the 5D2C9A reconstruction view, this is cooperative API containment, not a sandbox against reflection or malicious private-code access. No `_COMMITTED_RECEIPTS`, `_atomic_interval_history`, Action resolution, Target history, or publisher state is written. This does not authenticate the descriptor, install authoritative history, continue gameplay, or enable serialization/restoration. The original `reconstruct_initial_run_spot()` committed-boundary refusal and all global false readiness flags remain unchanged.
