+## 21. 5D2C11A private advanced-time Encounter construction
+
+`Encounter.__init__` continues to refuse ordinary `time != start_time` construction with its existing unsupported-migration invariant. A separate underscore-private constructor path, `Encounter._construct_quarantined_post_boundary()`, accepts only an internal validated plan for the exact `start_time=0`, `time=1`, two-native-Being case. It validates the isolated Universe registry and origin Event, participant identity/ownership, complete directed awareness references, no prior Universe scheduling/Event context, and a valid exclusive private caller RNG cursor before construction.
+
+The path initializes the Encounter at its captured start and advanced cursor in one constructor call; it does not create an Encounter at time zero and patch clock fields afterward. Native constructor invariants establish `last_processed_boundary=1`, `_coordinator_time=1`, `_interval_start=1`, no active boundary/fault/reentrancy, and a fresh ChoiceBook with empty drafts, choices, reservations, registration and lifecycle maps. It registers only the new Encounter Event in the private Universe, then quarantines the Encounter, Universe and participants before returning to its internal binder. The caller RNG stays private and unchanged; it is not attached as a progression mode.
+
+The 5D2C10 binder now uses this private path and exposes only a frozen `QuarantinedNativeEncounterView` with the clock, next boundary, participants, awareness, empty live queues/scheduler and private RNG state. The weak-keyed private binding keeps the native Encounter, Universe, Being instances, inert Action identity shells and RNG owner under one binding identity. The immutable binding result cross-links that identity through the Encounter/Being/Action logical IDs, historical Choice ID and Target-owned sidecar; each historical Action view and practice contribution retains its own Choice/Action/Target causal references. Historical Spot Actions remain inert detached identity objects and are not registered in the Event history, ChoiceBook, finished queue or receipt/history registries. The historical sidecar is not attached to the native Encounter. `step()`, `run()` and supported progression entry points remain blocked by quarantine. This adds a validated construction prerequisite only: it does not authenticate the data, restore or resume an Encounter, enable save/load or replay, attach historical outcomes, or change global checkpoint readiness flags.
