+## 22. 5D2C12C1 inert imported Spot practice input
+
+`src/frozen_practice.py` now provides `freeze_imported_spot_practice()` and `merge_imported_practice_uses()` as inactive data adapters. The first accepts only the existing exact quarantined one-boundary/two-Spot sidecar. It cross-checks the Target, Action, Choice and effect identities; exercise order and amounts; batch and transition totals/timing; the no-personal-history subset; and the projected post-boundary rank, baseline and skill experience. It converts both separate `PracticeExerciseProjection` causes to the existing frozen `CandidatePracticeUse`/`EffectIdentity` types, assembles one Target-owned `BatchSkillUse`, and routes it through the existing `_copy_use()` validator. It does not install that row into a Being or grant receipt authority.
+
+The returned `ImportedPracticePrefix/1` is frozen and contains only logical IDs, immutable practice data and a deterministic content digest. The digest is a future read-dependency token only; it is not a signature, authenticity claim or readiness certificate. The merge helper returns a detached tuple in the existing `FrozenBeingPractice.prior_uses` shape, followed by validated native suffix rows in chronological order. It rejects duplicate Action/skill causes, wrong Target ownership, stale prefix digest, unsupported practice variants, and suffix rows at or before the imported boundary. Current XP/ranks are passed through unchanged; imported exercise amounts are not summed into authoritative state again.
+
+The public `capture_practice_inputs(world, objects, entity_views)` signature and ordinary behavior remain unchanged. 5D2C12C5 adds a private prepared-context adapter that enters the same closed definition/history/use-copy validators and produces the same `FrozenPracticeInputs` and `FrozenBeingPractice` records, merging this prefix once into the Target's `prior_uses`. It does not apply XP or mutate native practice history, Target history, receipts, RNG, Action/Event/Choice registries, quarantine state, or Encounter progression. Personal-history-bearing imports, other Action families, multiple/imported boundaries and cross-process trust remain unsupported. Global `closure_validated`, `portable_schema_defined`, and `restore_verified` remain false.
